parliament welcomes italy's president  giorgio napolitano staunch europhile and  former mep talked about the importance  of the euro with just three months to go  before the european elections the  president also brought up the challenges  the eu has to tackle vis-a-vis winning  over young people  a reformed  facing strong opposition from several  member states and financial experts a  financial transaction tax negotiations  have been deadlocked for months there  has even been an about phase from some  of the countries who were initially in  favor of introducing the tax  it now looks unlikely that the text will  be adopted in 2014.  meps took stock of recent developments  in a debate with the council and  commission  commanders  it's estimated that financial  transaction tax could yield 30 to 35  billion euros a year  so far only 11 countries are set to  introduce ftt through enhanced  cooperation artists will enjoy better  protection from collecting societies in  europe with music often sold via  internet platforms it's difficult or  even impossible for artists to enforce  their rights and claim the money owed  from around europe  mep's approved multi-territorial  licensing which will be valid in all 28  member states  not only is this a step forward for  music providers consumers will also have  a much wider range of online music at  their fingertips  these reforms allow there to be much  greater transparency  in collection  of royalties on behalf of authors and  people who have created and thereby  allowing them to carry on developing  their creations  each year the music industry brings in 6  billion euros in europe
 

